From 0c9a1b5bea190ac00a59ae73aaa294abba9754df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Salveti <ricardo.salveti@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 20:46:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backend-drm: only put overlay planes on the per-output plane
 list

drm_output_find_plane_for_paint_node() asserts that every plane on
output->plane_handle_list is an overlay, but drm_output_init_planes()
puts every plane usable by the CRTC on that list, minus only the ones it
selects as the scanout and cursor planes. On hardware that advertises
more than one primary or cursor plane per CRTC, the spare ones stay on
the list and the assert fires as soon as a paint node becomes a
candidate for a hardware plane:

  state-propose.c:874: Assertion plane->type == WDRM_PLANE_TYPE_OVERLAY
  (1 == 2) failed!

A QCS9100 (SA8775P) Ride SX hits this on every EGL client. The DPU
driving its display exposes eight planes, six primary and two cursor,
all usable by every one of its six CRTCs, and no overlay planes at all.
With a single output enabled, five primary planes and one cursor plane
are left on the list, and the compositor aborts as soon as a client
posts a buffer.

The assert came with 96e9f4e4 ("drm: Remove switch in state-propose"),
which dropped the "case WDRM_PLANE_TYPE_PRIMARY: continue" that used to
skip these planes, on the grounds that only overlay planes are on the
list. Make that true. The spare primary and cursor planes go unused,
exactly as they did before 96e9f4e4.

Fixes: 96e9f4e4 ("drm: Remove switch in state-propose")
Signed-off-by: Ricardo Salveti <ricardo.salveti@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 libweston/backend-drm/drm.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libweston/backend-drm/drm.c b/libweston/backend-drm/drm.c
index c01cf387..d05db66a 100644
--- a/libweston/backend-drm/drm.c
+++ b/libweston/backend-drm/drm.c
@@ -2666,6 +2666,14 @@ drm_output_init_planes(struct drm_output *output)
 			output->cursor_handle = handle;
 			continue;
 		}
+
+		/* drm_output_find_plane_for_paint_node() asserts that every
+		 * plane on this list is an overlay, so keep the rest off it. */
+		if (plane->type != WDRM_PLANE_TYPE_OVERLAY) {
+			drm_plane_destroy_handle(handle);
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		wl_list_insert(&output->plane_handle_list, &handle->link);
 	}
 
